  "term": "abstract ability",
  "definition": "Abstract ability is a part of cognitive functioning that is assessed as one of the domains in the Montreal Cognitive Assessment. In this source, it is treated as a cognitive dimension alongside areas such as attention, language, delayed recall, and orientation.",
